Range binders recognize unary bodies without extra parentheses, while
ordinary calls of a function named forall retain their binary operators.

-- in.cue --
@test(json, [2, -1, false, 3], at="out")
a: forall (n in 1 | 2) >=n
a: 2
b: exists (n in 1 | 2) -n
b: -1
c: exists (v in true | false) !v
c: false
forall: func(x: int) -> int: x
x: 2
out: [a, b, c, forall(x) + 1]
